Nele and I are sitting at the table with our coffee this Tuesday morning.
My laptop is open between us.
We are discussing the big UI project.
We started it in the spring.
Back then, the work was still new and complicated.
Now the project is just normal everyday life.
Nele points at the screen.
"The design looks great already," she says.
"Yes, we are on a good path," I answer.
I take a sip of coffee and look out the window.
The trees outside have thick, green leaves.
"Do you remember, in January?" I ask Nele.
"The branches were completely bare and everything was grey."
"The new job was really daunting at first."
Nele nods and laughs.
"But you settled in very quickly," she says.
I smile and look back at the laptop.
"That's true," I say happily.
Then we continue working, relaxed.
